From 957684f809eae92f5c0ff0fe57f967cbd357ab23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:38:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/httpauth: do not put CR or LF into the Digest header

Fixes: CRLF injection
Fixes: avx3Qkpk8ANg
Fixes: digest_username_crlf_poc.py
Fixes: proxy_digest_uri_crlf_poc.py
CRLF injection Replicated through UnModified FFmpeg with a local TCP listener

Found during triage of the security report iUFdqPjbigVZ (ZDI-CAN-35984)

(cherry picked from commit 957684f809eae92f5c0ff0fe57f967cbd357ab23)
---
 libavformat/httpauth.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/httpauth.c b/libavformat/httpauth.c
index 4bc746dbf306..31160d598009 100644
--- a/libavformat/httpauth.c
+++ b/libavformat/httpauth.c
@@ -275,7 +275,8 @@ char *ff_http_auth_create_response(HTTPAuthState *state, const char *auth,
         if (!username)
             return NULL;
 
-        if ((password = strchr(username, ':'))) {
+        if ((password = strchr(username, ':')) &&
+            !strpbrk(username, "\r\n") && !strpbrk(path, "\r\n")) {
             *password++ = 0;
             authstr = make_digest_auth(state, username, password, path, method);
         }
